cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Least-Cost-Path: A Python tool for Least Cost Path analysis in archaeology"
abstract: "Least-Cost-Path (LCP) computes least-cost routes over raster friction surfaces for archaeology. Supports four analysis modes (all_pairs, single_origin, cross_layers, od_pair), two computation kernels (Dijkstra-based MCP_Geometric and a hierarchical directed A* corridor_astar), route densification and QGIS-style kernel density heatmaps, with two-phase parallel execution, resumable tracebacks and atomic GeoPackage outputs."
authors:
